.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-RESTORE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-restore - Restore an earlier policy version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy restore <version> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Save an earlier policy version as the new current version. The history keeps
every version, so a restore can itself be undone. When the restore changes
anyone's access, the changes are printed and must be confirmed; --yes confirms
them without asking. pb policy versions lists the versions.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for restore

.PP
\fB--message\fP=""
	describe the restore in the version history

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	confirm the printed access changes without asking


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy restore 3
  pb policy restore 3 --yes --message "undo"
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
